421:
A registry shall be kept of all persons practicing massage on the premises of such massage therapy establishment, which shall be available for inspection by an agent of the city during normal hours of business, providing the following information:
(1) Legal name and any other name(s) the licensed massage therapist has been or is known as or by;
(2) Current address including street and city;
(3) State or country of birth; date of birth;
(4) Number and expiration date of state license; and
(5) Position with the massage therapy establishment or business entity.
(Ord. No. 2013-34, 12-9-2013)

426:
Upon notice the city clerk may for good cause, revoke or suspend or place on probation the license of any massage therapy establishment/massage parlor;
(1) That commits or allows any violations of the provisions of this article of the City Code;
(2) That allows any massage therapist, working on the massage therapy establishment/massage parlor's premises, to commit or offer to commit a sexual crime under O.C.G.A. title 16, chapter 6;
(3) That allows any person to perform or offer massage on the premises who is not a licensed massage therapist;
(4) Where the applicant for the massage therapy establishment/massage parlor's city license gave false information on the application, in his or her affidavit, or in the massage therapy establishment/massage parlor's registry as required in this division, or fails to update information related to the license to the city clerk as required by this division; or
(5) Where the licensee fails at any time to meet the requirements for licensure under this division.
(6) Penalties: In addition to revocation or suspension of the massage therapy license, any person who violates any provision of this article may, upon conviction, be punished in accordance with the City of Fairburn Code. Each day during which said offenses occur shall constitute a separate offense, as shall each separate act constitute a violation.
(Ord. No. 2013-34, 12-9-2013)

