a. Exterior siding materials, excluding gables, soffits and minor trim, for the front of every building shall be 100 percent brick, stone or cementitious siding; each side shall be at least 40 percent brick, stone or cementitious siding; vinyl siding and metal siding is prohibited.
b. All proposed developments must adhere to the design standards in the Highway 74 Overlay District.
c. All buildings must have a permanent foundation, defined as a continuous perimeter base on which the building rests, to be constructed from masonry brick on a footing to be placed a minimum of 42 inches below the final ground level.
(Ord. No. 2024-04, § 1(Exh. A), 1-22-2024)
